From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apps_std: add bounded volatile phone files

Add a default-off backend for the two absolute paths whose write requests were
observed in run73. Existing read-only mappings remain unchanged. Only r/rb,
w/wb and a/ab are accepted for those paths. Reads can seed from a bounded VFS
snapshot; every mutation remains in independent process memory.

Handles use a generation-qualified namespace. Each file is capped at1MiB, each
operation at64KiB and the context at16 live handles. Failed grows preserve old
bytes, append recomputes position, seeks cannot be sparse, stale generations are
refused, and deinitialization frees all memory.

Method5 follows the pinned Qualcomm IDL and phone-library dispatch layout: two
inputs and one primary output, with bytesWritten and EOF. An optional listener
preflight rejects oversized RAM reads before output allocation. fread, fseek,
fflush and fclose route the reserved namespace. Normal-file writes and mapped
file statistics remain refused.

Tests exercise exact wire decoding, seeded and writable copies, cross-handle
visibility and cursors, truncation, append, read-only failures, malformed and
neighbor names, limits, allocation and generation failures, invalid seek, stale
handles and cleanup. No host writable path, partition, firmware load, DSP
executable or sensor stream is introduced. Daemon option -W is default-off.

